{"claims":[{"claim_text":"In the United States, the decades-long struggle for increased leisure time, weekends, and overtime pay culminated in congressional passage of the Fair Labor Standards Act (FLSA) in 1938.", "claim_types":["factual_assertion"],"evidence_ids":[1]},{"claim_text":"The eight-hour day became standard in the United States thanks to both union bargaining and the FLSA requirement of “time-and-a-half” pay for any hours worked in excess of 40 during a single week.", "claim_types":["factual_assertion"],"evidence_ids":[1]},{"claim_text":"Today, in the United States, the eight-hour day is being eroded as corporate CEOs continue their pursuit of profits at the expense of workers.", "claim_types":["factual_assertion"],"evidence_ids":[2]},{"claim_text":"Extra pay for overtime hours was intended to be a financial penalty, encouraging employers to expand their workforce rather than rely on overtime to meet production needs.", "claim_types":["factual_assertion"],"evidence_ids":[2]},{"claim_text":"When job-based benefits like health insurance began to bulk up labor costs, premium pay ceased to be a deterrent to overtime.", "claim_types":["factual_assertion"],"evidence_ids":[2]},{"claim_text":"It became cheaper for employers to schedule overtime than hire new workers.", "claim_types":["factual_assertion"],"evidence_ids":[2]},{"claim_text":"The failure of the Fair Labor Standards Act (FLSA) to establish limits on the working day or week has left Americans working more hours than in other advanced industrialized countries.", "claim_types":["factual_assertion"],"evidence_ids":[3]},{"claim_text":"Productivity increases while pay stagnates, forcing people to work additional hours, take second jobs, or max-out their credit cards in order to keep up with the rising cost of living.", "claim_types":["factual_assertion"],"evidence_ids":[3]},{"claim_text":"The erosion of leisure time undermines the founding principles of democracy.", "claim_types":["evaluation"],"evidence_ids":[3]},{"claim_text":"A capitalist system exploits workers instead of benefiting them.", "claim_types":["evaluation"],"evidence_ids":[3]}],"unresolved_references":[]}
```

